summarise

User selects
-date
-time slot
-guest count

Table Capacity
-table 1 → 8 people
-table 10–12 → 6 people
-others → 2–4 people

Table rule
-2 guests → table 2/4 only
-6 guests → table 6
-8 guests → table 8

Availability Logic
-find bookings
-where
-date = selectedDate
-timeSlot = selectedSlot

Pre-Order Flow
-Modal Stepper
    -Step 1: Pre-order? yes/no
    -Step 2: Menu selection
    -Step 3: Reservation summary

Payment Flow
-click confirm
  → server check booking exists
  → if not exist
  → create Stripe checkout
  → redirect
-If conflict happens:
  -duplicate booking detected
    1. refund payment
    2. show message
    3. send user back to booking page

Database Storage
- restaurant_db.booking
- schema
  -userId
  -tableId
  -date
  -timeSlot
  -guestCount
  -reservationCost
  -reservationFee
  -preOrderItems
  -stripeSessionId
  -status
- and the unique index:
  -tableId + date + timeSlot

Messaging System
- Admin → user message
- Example message:
  Reservation Confirmed
  Table: 5
  Date: March 20
  Time: 17:00–19:00
  Guests: 4
- If refund:
  Reservation Failed
  Table already booked.
  Refund will be processed automatically
  
Profile Page
-Table tab should show:
  -bookingId
  -date
  -timeSlot
  -table
  -status
-Cancel rule
  -cancel allowed until 3 hours before reservation

Admin Panel
- In booking tab shows detail of booking and 3 buttons:
    -Check In : user arrived
    -No Show  : user didn't arrive
    -Cancel : admin cancelled
- Refund rules:
  Check In → refund reservation cost
  No Show → no refund
  Cancel → refund preorder food only
- should I add all these booking status states?
  -confirmed
  -checked_in
  -no_show
  -cancelled
  -refund_pending
  -refunded

*Important Clarification
rule: table unavailable only after payment. This is correct but remember during Stripe payment 2 users can pay simultaneously
database unique index must enforce the final protection. Without that index, your system will break.

3 May 2026

==================================================
Week 1 - Quality + Reliability Foundation
==================================================

Day 1 - Baseline + Scope Lock
- [x] Freeze major feature changes for 2 weeks (except critical bugs) — optional discipline; KPI doc in next_update/change
- [x] Define success metrics (booking / payment / refund / API p95) — see next_update/change
- [x] Document KPI targets and scope — next_update/change + structured API logs + Analysis tab
Definition of done:
- [x] KPI list is clear and measurable

Day 2 - Unit Tests for Booking Rules
- [x] Add unit tests for table capacity rules (backend/test/bookingRules.test.js)
- [x] Add unit tests for reservation cost calculation
- [x] Add unit tests for cancellation cutoff (3-hour rule)
- [x] Add unit tests for booking status transition guard logic (admin actions from confirmed only)
Definition of done:
- [x] Unit test suite passes: run `npm test` from backend/

Day 3 - API Integration Tests
- [x] Test GET /api/bookings/availability (`test/integration/bookingApi.integration.test.js`)
- [x] Test POST /api/bookings/create-checkout-session (401/400/409 + mocked Stripe success)
- [x] Test POST /api/bookings/:id/cancel (confirm + happy path)
- [x] Test admin actions (check-in, no-show, cancel)
- [x] Add conflict test (same table/date/time — 409 + unique index)
Definition of done:
- [x] Integration tests pass with seeded deterministic data (`npm test` uses in-memory MongoDB)

Day 4 - Webhook Idempotency Hardening
- [x] Ensure duplicate Stripe webhook events are safe (`ProcessedStripeEvent` + booking intent pending-only)
- [x] Persist processed event IDs (`processed_stripe_events` collection; claim before handle, delete on 500)
- [x] Add duplicate webhook simulation test (`test/stripeWebhookDedupe.test.js`)
Definition of done:
- [x] Replayed webhook does not duplicate booking/refund side effects (same `event.id` short-circuits)

Day 5 - Refund Reconciliation Job
- [x] Implement job to scan refund_pending (`jobs/refundReconciliationJob.js` — Booking + BookingIntent)
- [x] Retry Stripe refunds from failed/pending records (`utils/stripeRefundPayment.js`)
- [x] Update DB status and send message notifications after retry
- [x] Add manual trigger command/script (`npm run refund:reconcile` from backend/)
Definition of done:
- [x] Pending refunds can be recovered automatically or by manual trigger

Day 6 - Load Test Baseline (k6)
- [x] Create k6 script for availability endpoint (`k6/booking-availability.js`)
- [x] Create k6 script for checkout-session endpoint (`k6/booking-checkout-session.js`)
- [x] Run normal load scenario (`K6_SCENARIO=normal` default — npm run k6:availability)
- [x] Run burst scenario (`npm run k6:availability:burst` / `k6:checkout:burst`)
- [x] Run race condition scenario (`npm run k6:availability:race` / `k6:checkout:race`)
Definition of done:
- [x] Baseline report exists — summary JSON + stdout (`http_req_duration` p95 via compactMetrics + failed rate); install k6, run scripts; outputs land in `k6/results/` (see `k6/results/README.txt`)